<.shell current={:field_definitions}>
  <h1>Field definitions</h1>
  <p class="lead">What each custom field on a team's records is, never its values.</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <.field_definitions
      id="field-definitions-sample"
      fields={custom_field_definitions()}
      team_names={%{11 => "Coast Range SAR"}}
      organization_name="WESARA"
      timezone="America/Vancouver"
      publish?
      restricted_text="Only team admins see its values."
    />
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    A Fields page in settings, for a team or an organization (#872). Each field shows its hint, its choices, who added it,
    and when. More than 8 choices show the first 3 and a count, which opens the rest, one per line. A choice a team
    added to its organization's field names the team. The fields in no group come first.
    Then each named group of fields follows under its title, as on a record's Fields tab.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    A record's own values. Those are the record's Fields tab, a <a href={page_path(:detail_list)}>detail list</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.field_definitions&gt;</code>
    takes one kind's fields, with their groups preloaded. Every column but Field fits
    its longest values, so each group's table lines up with the next. <code>copy?</code>
    adds who sees a member field and
    its Copy check box; <code>from?=&#123;false&#125;</code>
    drops the From column on an organization's page, where
    every field is its own.
  </p>
</.shell>
